<article class="env-lemma" id="0AFG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AFG">Lemma <span data-tag="0AFG">37.22.3</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of locally Noetherian schemes which is locally of finite type and Cohen-Macaulay. For every point $x$ in $X$ with image $y$ in $Y$, </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \dim _ x(X) = \dim _ y(Y) + \dim _ x(X_ y),  \]
</div>
  <p> where $X_ y$ denotes the fiber over $y$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      After replacing $X$ by an open neighborhood of $x$, there is a natural number $d$ such that all fibers of $X \to Y$ have dimension $d$ at every point, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02NM" data-tag="02NM">29.30.4</a>. Then $f$ is flat, locally of finite type and of relative dimension $d$. Hence the result follows from Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0AFE" data-tag="0AFE">29.30.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>